From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: huawei_gaokun: Set the orientation before DP

The driver sets the plug orientation only in its .connector_status()
callback, which UCSI calls once GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS for a connector
change has completed. The USB event from the EC carries the orientation
along with the mode and HPD state, but its handler only switches the QMP
PHY mode and notifies HPD, assuming the orientation has been set by then.

It may not have been. On a MateBook E Go, GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS sometimes
times out when a DP monitor is plugged in, and on port 1 UCSI got no
connector status at all. The PHY then keeps the orientation of the
previous plug, and if the monitor is plugged in the other way round,
link training fails:

  [drm:msm_dp_ctrl_link_train_1_2] *ERROR* max v_level reached
  [drm:msm_dp_ctrl_link_train_1_2] *ERROR* link training #1 on phy 0 failed. ret=-11
  [drm:msm_dp_bridge_atomic_enable] *ERROR* Failed link training (rc=-104)

followed by vblank timeouts until the monitor is unplugged. In ten plugs
with the plug flipped each time, UCSI had no connector status in time
for six; four of them failed this way, and the other two happened to
match the previous orientation. The four with a status all worked.

Set the orientation from the USB event before the mode and HPD. Do not
take the connector lock for it: UCSI holds the lock while it waits for a
command completion, which only the EC notifier thread can deliver. As
USB events are far more frequent than orientation changes, only update
the orientation when it has changed, which also saves the uevent.

Fixes: 00327d7f2c8c ("usb: typec: ucsi: add Huawei Matebook E Go ucsi driver")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c
index 2d8b249..45851aa 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c
@@ -180,6 +180,7 @@ static void gaokun_ucsi_update_connector(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 static void gaokun_set_orientation(struct ucsi_connector *con,
 				   struct gaokun_ucsi_port *port)
 {
+	enum typec_orientation orientation;
 	enum gaokun_ucsi_ccx ccx;
 	unsigned long flags;
 
@@ -187,7 +188,9 @@ static void gaokun_set_orientation(struct ucsi_connector *con,
 	ccx = port->ccx;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&port->lock, flags);
 
-	typec_set_orientation(con->port, CCX_TO_ORI(ccx));
+	orientation = CCX_TO_ORI(ccx);
+	if (typec_get_orientation(con->port) != orientation)
+		typec_set_orientation(con->port, orientation);
 }
 
 static void gaokun_ucsi_connector_status(struct ucsi_connector *con)
@@ -299,6 +302,7 @@ static int gaokun_ucsi_refresh(struct gaokun_ucsi *uec)
 static void gaokun_ucsi_handle_usb_mode(struct gaokun_ucsi_port *port)
 {
 	struct gaokun_ucsi *uec = port->ucsi;
+	struct ucsi_connector *con;
 	int idx = port->idx, ret;
 
 	/*
@@ -314,14 +318,32 @@ static void gaokun_ucsi_handle_usb_mode(struct gaokun_ucsi_port *port)
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Set the orientation from this event before the mode and HPD, so that
+	 * the PHY lanes match the plug when DP starts link training. The
+	 * .connector_status() callback sets it too, but only once UCSI's
+	 * GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS completes, which can be later or time out. Not
+	 * under the connector lock: in the EC notifier thread, UCSI may hold it
+	 * while waiting for a command completion that only this thread can
+	 * deliver. That leaves a small race with the callback: both set the
+	 * orientation from port->ccx, so they only disagree if the callback
+	 * read it just before this event changed it and writes after this, in
+	 * which case the orientation stays stale until the next event on the
+	 * port.
+	 */
+	if (idx < uec->ucsi->cap.num_connectors) {
+		con = &uec->ucsi->connector[idx];
+		if (con->port)
+			gaokun_set_orientation(con, port);
+	}
+
 	ret = typec_mux_set(port->typec_mux, &port->state);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(uec->dev, "failed to set mux %d\n", ret);
 
 	/*
-	 * UCSI callback .connector_status() have set orientation. Report HPD
-	 * while in DP alt mode, and once more when the port leaves it (unplug
-	 * or a switch to USB), or the connector stays connected.
+	 * Report HPD while in DP alt mode, and once more when the port leaves
+	 * it (unplug or a switch to USB), or the connector stays connected.
 	 */
 	if (port->bridge) {
 		bool hpd = port->svid == USB_TYPEC_DP_SID && port->hpd_state;
